course: world
lesson: 107
title: How long until? Counting on across the hour
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: "Muuum, how long till we get there?" It is 2:35 and they arrive at 3:10. Don't count minute by minute; jump like a frog on stepping stones. First jump to the o'clock: 2:35 to 3:00 is 25 minutes. Then jump the rest: 3:00 to 3:10 is 10 minutes. 25 + 10 = 35 minutes.
explain: Friendly times like :00 and :30 make good stepping stones. From 7:28 to 7:45: 2 minutes to 7:30, then 15 more, 17 minutes in all.
explain: Adding works the same way. Grace's cake needs 35 minutes from 4:40: 20 minutes takes you to 5:00, and the other 15 take you to 5:15. Split the minutes so you land on the o'clock first. With hours and minutes, add the hours first, then the minutes.
explain: Some sums run backwards from a deadline: to be at the airport 2 hours before a 10:15 flight, be there at 8:15; with a 45-minute drive, leave at 7:30. And don't forget the extras: a cinema's 20 minutes of adverts come before the film.
fact: To count on across the hour, jump to the next o'clock first, then add the extra minutes.
fact: From 2:35 to 3:10 is 35 minutes: 25 minutes to 3:00 and 10 more.
fact: From 7:28 to 7:45 is 17 minutes: 2 minutes to 7:30 and 15 more.
fact: To add minutes across the hour, split them: 4:40 + 35 minutes is 4:40 + 20 = 5:00, then + 15 = 5:15.
fact: To add hours and minutes, add the hours first: 5:50 + 1 hour 20 minutes is 6:50, then 7:10.
fact: To find when to leave, work back from the deadline: a 10:15 flight, 2 hours early at the airport, means 8:15; a 45-minute drive means leaving at 7:30.
fact: 11:50 + 1 hour 25 minutes = 1:15, which is after a 1:00 lunch.
fact: From 8:52 to 9:17 is 25 minutes, close to half an hour but 5 minutes short.
fact: Grown-ups often round to "half an hour", which is fine for chat but not for planning.
fact: Cinemas show adverts and trailers before the film, so a 6:40 ticket with 20 minutes of adverts and a 2-hour-5-minute film ends at 9:05.
fact: A washing machine screen showing 1:40 means 1 hour 40 minutes, so a wash started at 9:35 ends at 11:15.
fact: "Quarter to three" plus "an hour and a half" is 2:45 + 1 hour 30 minutes = 4:15.
fact: Words people use: "cos" means because, "wicked" means very (New England, USA), "yeah nah" means no (Australia, New Zealand), "sweet as" means great (New Zealand) "servo" means a petrol station (Australia), "sick" means great and "no cap" means "no lie".
exercise: It is 2:35 and Jayden's family arrives at 3:10. How long until they get there? | 35 minutes | 25 minutes | 45 minutes | 75 minutes
exercise: The match kicks off at 7:45. Darius gets home at 7:28. How long until kick-off? | 17 minutes | 23 minutes | 13 minutes | 27 minutes
exercise: Grace's cake goes in at 4:40 and needs 35 minutes. When is it ready? | 5:15 | 5:05 | 4:75 | 5:35
exercise: Ethan has 1 hour 20 minutes of screen time from 5:50. When must he stop? | 7:10 | 6:10 | 7:20 | 6:70
exercise: Mae's flight leaves at 10:15 and they must be at the airport 2 hours before. When must they arrive? | 8:15 | 12:15 | 9:15 | 8:45
exercise: They must be at the airport at 8:15 and the drive takes 45 minutes. When should they leave home? | 7:30 | 7:45 | 9:00 | 7:15
exercise: It is 11:50 and the update says 1 hour 25 minutes left. When will it finish? | 1:15 | 12:75 | 1:25 | 12:15
exercise: Harry's bus leaves at 8:52 and gets to school at 9:17. How long is the ride? | 25 minutes | 35 minutes | 30 minutes | 17 minutes
exercise: The film starts at 6:40, with 20 minutes of adverts and then 2 hours 5 minutes of film. When does it end? | 9:05 | 8:45 | 9:25 | 8:05
exercise: Kiara starts the wash at 9:35. The screen says 1:40. When will it finish? | 11:15 | 10:15 | 11:75 | 9:75
exercise: Finn's cousins land at quarter to three and then drive an hour and a half. When do they arrive? | 4:15 | 3:15 | 4:45 | 4:30
exercise: What is quarter to three in digital? | 2:45 | 3:15 | 3:45 | 2:15
exercise: What is the best first step when counting on from 8:52 to 9:17? | Jump to 9:00 first | Count every single minute | Take 52 away from 17 | Add 52 and 17 together
exercise: Why must a cinema pickup time include the adverts? | The film starts after the adverts, so it ends later | Adverts are shown after the film ends | Adverts make the film run faster | Pickups always happen at the start
exercise: How do you add 1 hour 20 minutes to a time? | Add the hour first, then the 20 minutes | Add 120 to the minutes | Add 20 hours and 1 minute | Add only the minutes and ignore the hour
test: Darius gets home at 7:28 for a 7:45 kick-off: "Plenty of time, yeah nah, I'll grab a snack first." How long has he really got? | 17 minutes | 45 minutes, till kick-off | Only 7 minutes | 1 hour 17 minutes
test: Grace's brother, starving: "Cake in at 4:40, 35 minutes, so it's ready at 4:75, innit?" Put him right. | 5:15, because there are only 60 minutes in an hour | 4:75 is right on a kitchen clock | 5:35, because you add the 40 and the 35 | 5:05, because you round down
test: Ruby: "Update says 1 hr 25 min and it's 11:50. Done for lunch at 1, no cap?" | No, it finishes at 1:15, 15 minutes after lunch starts | Yes, it finishes at 12:15 | Yes, it finishes at exactly 1:00 | No, it finishes at 2:15
test: Harry's friend says the bus from 8:52 to 9:17 takes "half an hour". What's true? | It takes 25 minutes, 5 short of half an hour | It takes exactly half an hour | It takes 35 minutes | It takes 17 minutes
test: Mae's dad in Boston: "Wicked early flight, 10:15, two hours at the airport, 45 to drive." When should they leave? | 7:30 | 8:15 | 7:15 | 9:30
test: What would happen if Zane's mum forgot the 20 minutes of adverts before his 6:40 film of 2 hours 5 minutes? | She would come at 8:45 and wait 20 minutes | She would come at 9:05, right on time | She would come at 9:25, very late | She would come at 7:00, at the start
test: Kiara's mum: "Hang the washing out when it's done, yeah?" It started at 9:35 and says 1:40. Kiara thinks 1:40 means 1:40 in the afternoon. Who's right? | 1:40 is how long it takes, so it ends at 11:15 | 1:40 is the time it ends, in the afternoon | 1:40 means 140 minutes, so 11:55 | 1:40 means 14 minutes, so 9:49
test: A Kiwi (New Zealand) aunt texts Finn: "Land quarter to three, then hour and a half drive, sweet as." When should he put his shoes on? | Just before 4:15 | Just before 2:45, when she lands | Around half past three | Not until about 5:45
test: Jayden asks "how long till we get there?" for the tenth time at 2:35; they arrive at 3:10. Dad snaps, "Ask again and we're turning round!" How long is left? | 35 minutes | 75 minutes | 45 minutes | 25 minutes
test: Ethan starts screen time at 5:50 with 1 hour 20 minutes and says, "Sick, I can play till 7:50." What's the real end? | 7:10 | 7:50 | 6:10 | 7:20
test: A cartoon cook says, "Ten past four plus fifty minutes is four sixty." Put it right. | It is 5:00 | It is 4:60, a real time | It is only 4:50 | It is 5:10 exactly
exam: It is given that a journey commences at 2:35 and concludes at 3:10. Determine the duration of the said journey. | Thirty-five minutes | Twenty-five minutes precisely | Some forty-five minutes | Seventy-five minutes
exam: Whereas a flight departs at 10:15, passengers are required at the airport two hours prior, and the drive occupies forty-five minutes, ascertain the latest time of departure from home. | 7:30 | 8:15 | 7:15 | 8:30
exam: A cinema performance commences at 6:40 with twenty minutes of advertisements preceding a film of two hours and five minutes. State the time of its conclusion. | 9:05 | 8:45 | 9:25 | 8:05
exam: Identify the method most consistent with established practice for counting on from 8:52 to 9:17. | Proceed to 9:00, then add the remaining seventeen minutes | Subtract fifty-two from seventeen | Add fifty-two to seventeen | Count each minute in reverse from 9:17
